WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.033 --> 00:00:00.633
So overnight.

00:00:00.633 --> 00:00:01.801
We're tracking breaking news

00:00:01.801 --> 00:00:02.635
out of Washington

00:00:02.635 --> 00:00:03.903
after Senate Minority Leader

00:00:03.903 --> 00:00:06.106
Mitch McConnell has been hospitalized

00:00:06.106 --> 00:00:06.873
after he tripped

00:00:06.873 --> 00:00:09.042
and fell at a hotel in Washington.

00:00:09.042 --> 00:00:10.010
I want to bring in our CNN

00:00:10.010 --> 00:00:12.112
congressional correspondent, Lauren Fox.

00:00:12.112 --> 00:00:13.346
Lauren, what do we know?

00:00:13.346 --> 00:00:15.248
What do we not know from McConnell's team

00:00:15.248 --> 00:00:17.283
so far about what happened?

00:00:17.283 --> 00:00:17.851
Yeah, what

00:00:17.851 --> 00:00:19.319
we know at this moment,

00:00:19.319 --> 00:00:20.520
Caitlin, is that

00:00:20.520 --> 00:00:21.087
he did

00:00:21.087 --> 00:00:22.188
suffer a fall

00:00:22.188 --> 00:00:24.290
at the Waldorf Astoria Hotel

00:00:24.557 --> 00:00:25.859
following a private dinner.

00:00:25.859 --> 00:00:26.793
I want to read

00:00:26.793 --> 00:00:28.228
this statement from his office

00:00:28.228 --> 00:00:29.729
saying this evening, Leader

00:00:29.729 --> 00:00:31.765
McConnell tripped at a local hotel

00:00:31.765 --> 00:00:33.099
during a private dinner.

00:00:33.099 --> 00:00:34.901
He has been admitted to the hospital

00:00:34.901 --> 00:00:37.203
where he is receiving treatment.

00:00:37.237 --> 00:00:39.305
Now, McConnell is 81 years old.

00:00:39.305 --> 00:00:41.741
He's the top Republican in the U.S.

00:00:41.741 --> 00:00:43.343
Senate and the longest

00:00:43.343 --> 00:00:45.845
serving Republican leader in that body.

00:00:46.112 --> 00:00:46.980
But there's just a lot

00:00:46.980 --> 00:00:48.181
we don't know right now

00:00:48.181 --> 00:00:49.482
about his condition,

00:00:49.482 --> 00:00:50.283
about how long

00:00:50.283 --> 00:00:51.618
he'll have to be at the hospital.

00:00:51.618 --> 00:00:53.686
It also comes at a time, Caitlin,

00:00:53.686 --> 00:00:55.388
when the Senate is narrowly

00:00:55.388 --> 00:00:56.523
divided right now

00:00:56.523 --> 00:00:58.558
and there are two Democratic senators

00:00:58.792 --> 00:01:00.827
who are also out for health reasons.

00:01:00.860 --> 00:01:02.695
You have Senator Dianne Feinstein,

00:01:02.695 --> 00:01:03.930
who is dealing with shingles.

00:01:03.930 --> 00:01:06.266
You also have Senator John Fetterman,

00:01:06.266 --> 00:01:07.434
the Pennsylvania Democrat

00:01:07.434 --> 00:01:08.802
who is receiving treatment

00:01:08.802 --> 00:01:10.203
for clinical depression

00:01:10.203 --> 00:01:11.571
at Walter Reed right now.

00:01:11.571 --> 00:01:12.372
So, you know,

00:01:12.372 --> 00:01:13.606
there's just a lot of questions.

00:01:13.606 --> 00:01:14.674
I will keep you updated

00:01:14.674 --> 00:01:16.776
as we get more information this morning.

00:01:16.776 --> 00:01:17.410
But right now,

00:01:17.410 --> 00:01:18.011
what we know

00:01:18.011 --> 00:01:19.813
is that McConnell suffered a fall

00:01:19.813 --> 00:01:20.413
last night

00:01:20.413 --> 00:01:21.948
and was hospitalized

00:01:21.948 --> 00:01:23.683
after that fell silent.

00:01:23.683 --> 00:01:24.617
He's obviously in our thoughts.

00:01:24.617 --> 00:01:26.352
We're hoping for a quick recovery

00:01:26.352 --> 00:01:26.953
for him.

00:01:26.953 --> 00:01:27.720
But, Lauren, in the broader

00:01:27.720 --> 00:01:28.888
impact of what this means is

00:01:28.888 --> 00:01:30.123
we've had these conversations

00:01:30.123 --> 00:01:32.292
when Senator Fetterman was hospitalized.

00:01:32.292 --> 00:01:33.093
Senator Feinstein,

00:01:33.093 --> 00:01:34.427
what does it mean for Senate

00:01:34.427 --> 00:01:35.662
leadership, given

00:01:35.662 --> 00:01:36.896
if he does

00:01:36.896 --> 00:01:39.332
need quite some time to recover

00:01:39.332 --> 00:01:40.500
Well, I think there's just a lot

00:01:40.500 --> 00:01:41.568
we don't know right now.

00:01:41.568 --> 00:01:43.002
But obviously, it's a narrowly

00:01:43.002 --> 00:01:43.970
divided body.

00:01:43.970 --> 00:01:44.671
It is a body

00:01:44.671 --> 00:01:45.305
in which

00:01:45.305 --> 00:01:47.807
McConnell has a lot of jurisdiction

00:01:48.074 --> 00:01:49.409
over his conference.

00:01:49.409 --> 00:01:50.343
He is somebody

00:01:50.343 --> 00:01:51.377
who is revered

00:01:51.377 --> 00:01:53.012
within his conference, trusted

00:01:53.012 --> 00:01:54.414
someone that lawmakers

00:01:54.414 --> 00:01:55.815
go to for advice,

00:01:55.815 --> 00:01:56.883
someone who decides

00:01:56.883 --> 00:01:58.651
the Republican strategy in the U.S.

00:01:58.651 --> 00:01:58.985
Senate.

00:01:58.985 --> 00:02:01.020
So obviously, his absence

00:02:01.020 --> 00:02:02.255
for any period of time

00:02:02.255 --> 00:02:03.456
will have an impact

00:02:03.456 --> 00:02:05.425
on the Republican conference.

00:02:05.425 --> 00:02:06.993
Of course, you also have Senator

00:02:06.993 --> 00:02:08.928
John Thune, who is the next in line.

00:02:08.928 --> 00:02:11.131
He is the Republican whip who,

00:02:11.131 --> 00:02:11.397
you know,

00:02:11.397 --> 00:02:13.366
would be expected to fill that vacuum.

00:02:13.366 --> 00:02:15.235
But we just don't know right now

00:02:15.235 --> 00:02:16.736
how long McConnell

00:02:16.736 --> 00:02:18.238
would be hospitalized for

00:02:18.238 --> 00:02:20.607
and how serious of a fall this was.

00:02:20.607 --> 00:02:21.274
Caitlin.

00:02:21.274 --> 00:02:22.876
All right. Lauren Fox, keep us updated.

00:02:22.876 --> 00:02:24.310
Thank you so much.

00:02:24.310 --> 00:02:25.345
I want to bring in CNN's

00:02:25.345 --> 00:02:26.946
political commentator Errol Louis

00:02:26.946 --> 00:02:29.282
for more on this Errol, obviously, we are

00:02:29.315 --> 00:02:30.350
we don't know a lot.

00:02:30.350 --> 00:02:31.518
We're hoping to learn more

00:02:31.518 --> 00:02:32.852
and we're wishing for the best

00:02:32.852 --> 00:02:34.454
for Senator McConnell.

00:02:34.454 --> 00:02:36.456
But this does have a significant impact

00:02:36.456 --> 00:02:38.525
potentially on how things work

00:02:38.525 --> 00:02:39.092
in Washington

00:02:39.092 --> 00:02:39.859
for any senator,

00:02:39.859 --> 00:02:41.961
but especially one is powerful

00:02:41.961 --> 00:02:43.863
in his caucus as Mitch McConnell.

00:02:43.863 --> 00:02:44.731
Oh, for sure.

00:02:44.731 --> 00:02:45.665
We should keep in mind

00:02:45.665 --> 00:02:46.833
that it is still a closely

00:02:46.833 --> 00:02:47.700
divided Senate.

00:02:47.700 --> 00:02:48.902
We had the vice president

00:02:48.902 --> 00:02:49.202
come in

00:02:49.202 --> 00:02:50.570
and break some ties

00:02:50.570 --> 00:02:52.038
on judicial nominations

00:02:52.038 --> 00:02:53.940
of no particular moment.

00:02:53.940 --> 00:02:55.842
That's how closely

00:02:55.842 --> 00:02:57.076
we still have to keep in mind.

00:02:57.076 --> 00:02:59.245
51 49 is nothing to sneeze at.

00:02:59.245 --> 00:02:59.812
And all it takes

00:02:59.812 --> 00:03:01.748
is one or two to be incapacitated

00:03:01.748 --> 00:03:03.016
or not in the chamber.

00:03:03.016 --> 00:03:03.750
And all of a sudden,

00:03:03.750 --> 00:03:04.984
a lot of things can change.

00:03:04.984 --> 00:03:06.753
But I think your larger point, though,

00:03:06.753 --> 00:03:09.255
the the interesting thing about McConnell

00:03:09.255 --> 00:03:09.722
is that

00:03:09.722 --> 00:03:11.191
we don't know where the Senate would go

00:03:11.191 --> 00:03:11.791
without him.

00:03:11.791 --> 00:03:12.659
He's you know, he's

00:03:12.659 --> 00:03:13.259
the longest

00:03:13.259 --> 00:03:15.061
serving Republican leader in history.

00:03:15.061 --> 00:03:16.863
And where they might go,

00:03:16.863 --> 00:03:17.564
you look at somebody

00:03:17.564 --> 00:03:18.565
like Senator Rick Scott,

00:03:18.565 --> 00:03:20.099
who made an abortive challenge to

00:03:20.099 --> 00:03:21.901
maybe take the leadership away.

00:03:21.901 --> 00:03:23.670
And he put forward some policies

00:03:23.670 --> 00:03:25.305
that were dramatically unpopular

00:03:25.305 --> 00:03:26.673
and was sort of shunted aside

00:03:26.673 --> 00:03:27.240
and so forth.

00:03:27.240 --> 00:03:28.641
But we don't know where that conference

00:03:28.641 --> 00:03:29.108
would go

00:03:29.108 --> 00:03:30.410
without the leadership of Mitch

00:03:30.410 --> 00:03:31.010
McConnell.

00:03:31.010 --> 00:03:31.878
We may find out.

00:03:31.878 --> 00:03:33.846
Find out in the next few weeks.

00:03:33.846 --> 00:03:34.447
Oh, sorry.

00:03:34.447 --> 00:03:35.782
Is there anything that they're working on

00:03:35.782 --> 00:03:37.917
now that would be in jeopardy

00:03:37.917 --> 00:03:40.220
because of a Mitch McConnell absence

00:03:40.320 --> 00:03:41.821
that is of critical importance

00:03:41.821 --> 00:03:42.422
at this moment?

00:03:42.422 --> 00:03:42.822
I think

00:03:42.822 --> 00:03:44.057
I think, you know, broadly

00:03:44.057 --> 00:03:44.657
speaking, trying

00:03:44.657 --> 00:03:45.325
to figure out

00:03:45.325 --> 00:03:46.793
what the strategy is going to be.

00:03:46.793 --> 00:03:48.361
I mean, you know, Senator Biden

00:03:48.361 --> 00:03:50.363
I mean, I should say President Biden is

00:03:50.563 --> 00:03:51.864
is is putting together

00:03:51.864 --> 00:03:53.132
and getting ready to announce

00:03:53.132 --> 00:03:54.534
he's making a speech today

00:03:54.534 --> 00:03:55.802
that is going to really,

00:03:55.802 --> 00:03:57.804
I think, sort of lay the groundwork,

00:03:57.804 --> 00:03:58.571
set the table

00:03:58.571 --> 00:04:00.707
for an announcement for president.

00:04:00.707 --> 00:04:02.609
Where are the Republicans going to go?

00:04:02.609 --> 00:04:03.843
What's their answer going to be?

00:04:03.843 --> 00:04:05.712
There's a relative amount of chaos

00:04:05.712 --> 00:04:06.946
over on the House side.

00:04:06.946 --> 00:04:07.680
And so you would

00:04:07.680 --> 00:04:08.715
try and look to the Senate.

00:04:08.715 --> 00:04:09.816
What are the policies

00:04:09.816 --> 00:04:11.384
that we're going to pick on again?

00:04:11.384 --> 00:04:12.118
You know,

00:04:12.185 --> 00:04:13.319
Senator Scott talks about,

00:04:13.319 --> 00:04:14.254
you know, budget

00:04:14.254 --> 00:04:16.923
deficit reduction and it's strayed into

00:04:17.023 --> 00:04:18.458
maybe we need to cut Medicare,

00:04:18.458 --> 00:04:20.159
maybe we need to cut Social Security.

00:04:20.159 --> 00:04:22.729
Third, rail in politics, a disaster

00:04:22.862 --> 00:04:24.097
sort of swept aside.

00:04:24.097 --> 00:04:26.199
Where do they go now? We don't know.

00:04:26.199 --> 00:04:27.166
I just was going to say,

00:04:27.166 --> 00:04:27.800
I mean, obviously,

00:04:27.800 --> 00:04:30.036
we know the longest serving, you know,

00:04:30.036 --> 00:04:31.804
Senate Republican leader in history,

00:04:31.804 --> 00:04:33.840
but also an important voice this week

00:04:33.840 --> 00:04:35.942
following that Fox News

00:04:35.942 --> 00:04:38.411
report, trying to whitewash January six

00:04:38.411 --> 00:04:39.212
when he came out.

00:04:39.212 --> 00:04:40.813
What he said,

00:04:40.847 --> 00:04:41.781
just, you know,

00:04:41.781 --> 00:04:43.549
thinking about that in the context of.

00:04:43.549 --> 00:04:44.050
Sure.

00:04:44.050 --> 00:04:44.851
I mean, this is now

00:04:44.851 --> 00:04:45.785
this is what the Senate is

00:04:45.785 --> 00:04:46.586
and this is what the Senate

00:04:46.586 --> 00:04:47.487
is supposed to be.

00:04:47.487 --> 00:04:48.087
You know,

00:04:48.154 --> 00:04:49.389
the median age in the US

00:04:49.389 --> 00:04:51.624
Senate is close to 65.

00:04:51.991 --> 00:04:54.627
There are a lot of older members there,

00:04:54.761 --> 00:04:56.062
but they represent and,

00:04:56.062 --> 00:04:56.262
you know,

00:04:56.262 --> 00:04:57.397
whatever their politics

00:04:57.397 --> 00:04:57.930
they represent

00:04:57.930 --> 00:05:00.233
sort of institutional continuity,

00:05:00.233 --> 00:05:02.368
a sort of way of cooling off

00:05:02.368 --> 00:05:04.504
some of the passions that are dividing

00:05:04.504 --> 00:05:05.905
the nation and so forth.

00:05:05.905 --> 00:05:07.907
And we already saw

00:05:07.907 --> 00:05:08.941
just a little bit of that.

00:05:08.941 --> 00:05:09.509
You know,

00:05:09.509 --> 00:05:10.310
the whole question

00:05:10.310 --> 00:05:12.645
of trying to relitigate January 6th

00:05:12.645 --> 00:05:13.713
and this attack,

00:05:13.713 --> 00:05:14.113
you know,

00:05:14.113 --> 00:05:15.548
you're relying on elders

00:05:15.548 --> 00:05:17.650
like Mitch McConnell to say, again,

00:05:17.650 --> 00:05:18.885
even if you don't like his politics

00:05:18.885 --> 00:05:19.886
and stand up and say,

00:05:19.886 --> 00:05:22.155
no, that was a disaster.

00:05:22.188 --> 00:05:23.523
That was something where

00:05:23.523 --> 00:05:24.924
we're going to stick to the facts.

00:05:24.924 --> 00:05:26.492
We're not going to see a repeat of this.

00:05:26.492 --> 00:05:27.994
We have to safeguard

00:05:27.994 --> 00:05:29.462
the institutions of the country.

00:05:29.462 --> 00:05:30.163
Yeah, and you're right.

00:05:30.163 --> 00:05:30.663
He's saying that

00:05:30.663 --> 00:05:31.497
what it was

00:05:31.497 --> 00:05:32.165
it was critical

00:05:32.165 --> 00:05:32.598
what he

00:05:32.598 --> 00:05:33.666
what Mitch McConnell said, that

00:05:33.666 --> 00:05:34.967
he's standing by police

00:05:34.967 --> 00:05:36.235
and the police assessment

00:05:36.235 --> 00:05:37.603
and rather than the Fox News

00:05:37.603 --> 00:05:38.838
assessment front of the cameras.

